# This repository IS the published website — github.com/TimColeX/eventually is
# public and serves eventually-app.com. So the rule is simple: if it shouldn't be
# readable by a stranger, or a browser never asks for it, it doesn't belong here.

# The old upload staging copy. Git replaces it — you now push from this folder
# directly, so keeping a second copy in sync is exactly the step that used to
# drop files silently.
Eventually-site/

# Server-side work. The SQL and Edge Functions contain no secrets, but they are
# the shape of the backend and there is no reason to publish them. They're
# deployed with the Supabase CLI, never served to a browser.
backend/
supabase/

